<http://data.silknow.org/object/44a7b7d0-70ca-358e-a6ee-4e804ac62c48/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Evening bodice and skirt of silk with satin stripes and large scale leaf pattern and bands of green stripes.\n\nThe bodice is trimmed with frills of pin silk gauze with scallop embroidered edges. The right shoulder has a curling ostrich feather mount. It is lined with linen with a vernacular pattern, boned and with a wide grosgrain waist band. It laces at the back.\n\nThe skirt has a pink satin pattern in the centre with pink chiffon drapes trimmed with pink ostrich feathers (Struthio camelus). It hooks at the back where it is gathered into a bustle. The front is lined with linen and the back with tarlatan. The sides are hooked over with elastic straps to form the bustle drape. The hem is satin-faced and there is a double tiered brush frill."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/44a7b7d0-70ca-358e-a6ee-4e804ac62c48> .

